# Applies to the obsidian-vault image only, which builds from the REPOSITORY
# ROOT because it compiles vault-mcp's Go source into itself. Without this the
# whole history and every document in the repo would be sent to the daemon on
# every build. (The other two stacks build from their own directories —
# `context: ./vault-mcp` and `context: ./dashboard` — and a .dockerignore at the
# root does not reach them.)
#
# Nothing listed here is copied by any Dockerfile, with ONE exception, spelled
# out below — check before adding to it.
.git
.github
bin
**/*.md
**/.env
**/.env.*

# The exception. research-CLAUDE.md is markdown by content but is not
# documentation: the image installs it as <scratch>/CLAUDE.md, the research
# agent's standing instructions. Excluded by **/*.md above, it is missing from
# the build context and the COPY fails the build outright — which is how this
# line came to exist.
#
# Keep this in step with build-obsidian-vault.yml, which filters markdown out of
# its trigger paths for the same reason this file excludes it, and needs the
# same exception. A change here that only lands in one of the two files gives an
# image whose agent instructions silently lag the repo.
!obsidian-vault/research-CLAUDE.md

# research-JOBS.md is the same case: the image installs it as <scratch>/JOBS.md,
# the contract both agents follow to hand a research job across. Same pairing
# with build-obsidian-vault.yml, same failure if only one of the two is updated.
!obsidian-vault/research-JOBS.md
